  _csoundFileGUID: fc128f30d914c44a6976034ccc93566d
  _csoundString: "<CsoundSynthesizer>\n<CsOptions>\n</CsOptions>\n<CsInstruments>\n\n;
    The clip, straight back out. This instance takes its AudioSource's clip as input,
    with Process\n; Audio Clip ON, so what Csound reads here is what Unity decided
    to hand the filter callback: the\n; clip's own 330 Hz, resampled by whatever
    Unity does to the playback rate. That is the one way a\n; Doppler shift can reach
    Csound at all, and this instrument does nothing that would hide it.\n\nksmps 
    = 32\nnchnls = 2\n0dbfs  = 1\n\ninstr 1\n  aL, aR ins\n  outs aL, aR\nendin\n\n</CsInstruments>\n<CsScore>\nf0
    z\ni 1 0 -1\n</CsScore>\n</CsoundSynthesizer>\n"
  _csoundFileName: DopplerPassThrough.csd
  _csoundAsset: {fileID: 102900000, guid: fc128f30d914c44a6976034ccc93566d, type: 3}
